  "verbalization": "Myxotyroside B appears to exert its biological effects through a series of mechanistic steps that ultimately target HepG2 cells. The evidence suggests that Myxotyroside B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine and 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether, which in turn inhibit HepG2. These compounds are likely acting through shared or distinct pathways, with the final target of all these entities being HepG2. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, suggesting that the observed effects are biologically relevant. The integration of these pathways implies that Myxotyroside B may modulate cellular processes that are critical for HepG2 survival, potentially through the inhibition of key molecular targets. The presence of multiple targets and their shared outcome in HepG2 suggests a possible role in cellular regulation, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
